# The app's version, in the style of .coverage-floor: THE one place it is
# stated. Everything that has to agree reads it from here.
#
#   scripts/bundle-app.sh   stamps CFBundleShortVersionString and
#                           CFBundleVersion into the bundle's Info.plist, so
#                           the About panel, the diagnostics bundle
#                           (DiagnosticsSnapshot.AppSection.version) and the
#                           ASC MHL creatorinfo all report this number.
#   scripts/release-notes.sh  picks the matching CHANGELOG.md section.
#   .github/workflows/release.yml  refuses to publish unless the tag that
#                           triggered it is exactly "v" + this number.
#
# Releasing: bump this, add the matching "## <version>" section to
# CHANGELOG.md, commit, then tag v<version>. The workflow fails loudly rather
# than shipping a bundle whose plist disagrees with the tag on the download.
#
# MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH, digits only — bundle-app.sh rejects anything else, because
# CFBundleShortVersionString has to be a plain version string for macOS.
#
# Still pre-1.0 deliberately: the v210 (10-bit YCbCr) capture path has never
# run against a board, and R3D is only real in a build made against RED's
# SDK. 0.1.0 was the never-tagged number the plist carried
# through development; the first published build takes its own so a
# diagnostics bundle can never be ambiguous about which is which.
0.2.0
